+| `InvalidConsentChannelError` | Thrown by `recordConsent` for a channel outside `CONSENT_CHANNELS` |
 
 ## Tables (`schema.ts`)
 
 | Table | Personal columns |
 |---|---|
 | `identity.person` | `email`, `given_name`, `family_name` |
+| `identity.consent` | `channel`, `granted`, `decided_at` |
 
 ## Events
 
 | Event | Direction | Payload |
 |---|---|---|
 | `identity.person-registered` | Emits | `personId`, `brand` |
+| `identity.consent-changed` | Emits, once per consent record | `personId`, `consentId`, `purpose`. Read the decision with `currentConsent` |
 
 ## Invariants
 
 - One person record per e-mail address. The e-mail is stored in lower case (T3-AC-003).
 - At most one ERP customer number per person (T3-AC-003).
+- Consent records are append-only: never changed or deleted. A new decision, including a withdrawal, adds a record. The latest record per person and purpose is the current decision (T3-AC-004).
+- A consent record belongs to an existing person.
 - ERP master data comes through the `integration` module, never from the ERP port.
 
 ## Acceptance criteria
